1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,770
Three AI agents, one repo.

2
00:00:01,770 --> 00:00:04,426
Two of them just rewrote the same file.

3
00:00:04,426 --> 00:00:07,490
One version is gone, and nothing recorded it.

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,159
This is Bullpen.

5
00:00:11,159 --> 00:00:13,261
Source control for AI agents.

6
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:15,519
One ask.

7
00:00:15,519 --> 00:00:18,374
The orchestrator splits it into three tasks,

8
00:00:18,374 --> 00:00:20,839
and three Claude Code agents walk onto

9
00:00:20,839 --> 00:00:22,851
campus, each on its own branch.

10
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:26,439
Two agents want auth.ts.

11
00:00:26,439 --> 00:00:28,177
The first one takes the lock.

12
00:00:28,177 --> 00:00:29,856
The second waits at the door

13
00:00:29,856 --> 00:00:31,234
until the file is free.

14
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:37,673
The database agent reaches for the schema.

15
00:00:37,673 --> 00:00:39,200
The referee, a Jetson on

16
00:00:39,200 --> 00:00:40,346
the desk, says no.

17
00:00:40,346 --> 00:00:42,000
The agent reads the reason

18
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:43,336
and changes its plan.

19
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:47,846
Don't like what one agent did?

20
00:00:47,846 --> 00:00:49,199
Undo that agent alone.

21
00:00:49,199 --> 00:00:50,799
Its commits roll back, and

22
00:00:50,799 --> 00:00:52,275
the others keep working.

23
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:56,073
Happy with another?

24
00:00:56,073 --> 00:00:58,219
Open its building, read the real diff,

25
00:00:58,219 --> 00:01:00,308
and merge through an intent card that

26
00:01:00,308 --> 00:01:01,776
says what changed and why.

27
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:06,919
Now pull the Jetson's cable.

28
00:01:06,919 --> 00:01:08,700
The referee is offline, so

29
00:01:08,700 --> 00:01:10,139
every edit is denied.

30
00:01:10,139 --> 00:01:11,578
Bullpen fails closed.

31
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:17,314
Under the pixels, everything is real.

32
00:01:17,314 --> 00:01:19,691
An agent takes a file lock before each

33
00:01:19,691 --> 00:01:22,693
edit, and the lock expires after ninety seconds.

34
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:25,480
Point Bullpen at any repo

35
00:01:25,480 --> 00:01:27,019
and it builds your campus.

36
00:01:27,019 --> 00:01:28,617
Each edit becomes a commit,

37
00:01:28,617 --> 00:01:29,919
tagged with its agent.

38
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:33,707
It runs on your own Claude

39
00:01:33,707 --> 00:01:35,677
subscription, with no API key.

40
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:39,640
The referee runs on separate

41
00:01:39,640 --> 00:01:41,572
hardware the agents cannot reach.

42
00:01:41,572 --> 00:01:44,208
Small on-device models write the history, and

43
00:01:44,208 --> 00:01:46,023
a secret guard scans each diff.

44
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:50,151
Anthropic rebuilt source control for

45
00:01:50,151 --> 00:01:51,823
agents, and called it Scion.

46
00:01:51,823 --> 00:01:54,093
Bullpen brings that to every engineer.

47
00:01:54,093 --> 00:01:55,527
Git tracks what changed.

48
00:01:55,527 --> 00:01:58,155
Bullpen controls who's allowed to change it.
